From: Zygote project
Subject: llama.cpp: enable LFM2 recurrent-state rollback for KV-prefix caching

LFM2.5 (Gated DeltaNet hybrid) needs per-token recurrent-state rollback
snapshots for partial KV-cache erasure, which is what the native prompt-
prefix cache relies on to trim divergent tails between turns. Default
n_rs_seq=0 makes llama_memory_seq_rm fail for any partial trim, silently
killing prefix caching. This is a local build change, not an upstream
contribution.

--- a/src/llama-arch.cpp
+++ b/src/llama-arch.cpp
@@ -1001,6 +1001,10 @@ bool llm_arch_supports_rs_rollback(const llm_arch & arch) {
         case LLM_ARCH_QWEN35:
         case LLM_ARCH_QWEN35MOE:
         case LLM_ARCH_DEEPSEEK4:
+        // Local build: LFM2 (Gated DeltaNet hybrid) needs recurrent-state
+        // rollback for KV-prefix reuse (multi-turn prompt caching on-device).
+        case LLM_ARCH_LFM2:
+        case LLM_ARCH_LFM2MOE:
             return true;
         default:
             return false;
